WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.500
Speaker 1: Today, I'm going to talk about
a topic that comes up often in discussions

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.460
around systemic change and individual personal
responsibility.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.559
I got an email over the weekend and this is
why I'm even talking about this today.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:20.360
The email said, Hey David Cuban American Streamer
Destiny, also known to some in our audience

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.710
is Steven Kenneth Destiny Bunnell.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:30.390
The second was recently interviewed and Destiny
said it's not hypocritical to on the one hand

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.520
say, hey, we need these systemic changes.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:39.480
But on the other hand, to encourage people
to take responsibility and give advice that

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:46.370
tells people individually how to best solve
their situation, even if you're not making

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.430
the systemic change.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.680
Now, I haven't been able to find the clip.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.270
Doesn't even really matter because this is
a very important topic and I want to talk

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:57.970
about it today because people have said to
me, I get emails, you know, when we do segments

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:02.090
on the finance, channel, channel, or people
call in during live calls with personal finance

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.049
questions or whatever the case may be.

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:10.049
People write to me, they'll say, David, how
can you, in good conscience and in good faith,

00:01:10.049 --> 00:01:15.380
advise people about how to reduce their own
tax liability, for example, or work to reduce

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:20.020
your own, but to advocate for higher taxes
for some people?

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:26.500
Or another example recently that came up,
I spoke about funding a 529 college savings

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.049
account or educational savings account for
my baby daughter.

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:33.939
And people say, How can you participate in
creating a 529 account for your baby daughter

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:38.541
while saying a huge problem is that college
education is too expensive, there are too

00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:43.119
many student loans, The stock market is not
accessible to everyone.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:45.790
Maybe college education should be less important.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:50.899
I'm going to address those specific questions,
but let's first set this up properly.

00:01:50.899 --> 00:01:53.140
Many people on the right.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:59.509
And even some on the left will argue there's
a hypocrisy to demanding systemic change while

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:03.860
encouraging people to take responsibility
for their own lives and to do what is best

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.750
for them in the moment.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.610
Some will say, and they say it to me, If you
believe in the systemic change, then you should

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:16.209
wait for the government to fix the problem
and not bother trying to improve your situation.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:23.260
Others might argue when you do what is best
for you, it actually will delay the systemic

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.900
solution that you might be calling for.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.890
This is a very flawed and sometimes absurd
argument.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:36.050
First of all, demanding a systemic change
and encouraging individual action are not

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.050
mutually exclusive.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.819
In fact, I would argue they go hand in hand.

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:42.750
Imagine, we want to see a more equal society.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.180
We would like to see a government policy to
reduce inequality in society.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:52.180
Well, we need to demand policies that address
systemic inequality like a living wage and

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:54.280
affordable housing and universal health care.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.490
And we should vote for candidates who will
do those things or who say they will do those

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.490
things.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:04.330
But at the same time, why wouldn't I encourage
people to educate themselves about how things

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:09.650
are today, how things work today to improve
their skills, to advocate for rights in the

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.120
marketplace, to take advantage of the tools
that are available to them, which they might

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.680
not even know about to improve their lives.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.989
Today, as we work to elect officials who will
make the bigger systemic change.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:26.970
Secondly, for me, as a progressive, demanding
systemic change is not about giving up personal

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:27.970
responsibility.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.260
It's about acknowledging Here's all the things
I can do.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:36.800
But there is a superstructure, a systemic
reality that is above and beyond what I can

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:37.800
do.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.620
It doesn't mean I don't do the things I can
do.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.250
It means I understand there's a second layer
to it.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:46.849
Some on the right like to say, Listen, you
want health care for all so that you, David,

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:50.120
as a self-employed person, don't have to buy
your own health care.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.580
That's what I do right now.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.269
Sure, maybe.

00:03:53.269 --> 00:03:58.439
But I'm going to get myself health care because
I need health care.

00:03:58.439 --> 00:04:05.000
It's not really about whether I am getting
health care on the marketplace, the healthcare.gov,

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.810
while saying everybody should get it.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.450
These are two different things.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:13.480
We're all products of our environment and
our choices are limited by the opportunities

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.970
and obstacles that exist systemically.

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:19.660
But within that, we should still do what we
can do to improve our situation.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:25.560
And if we want to empower people to succeed,
we should create a society that provides equal

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:30.020
opportunity when it comes to education and
health care and other economic opportunities.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.919
Last thing.

00:04:31.919 --> 00:04:36.080
Encouraging individual action also doesn't
mean we ignored the systemic inequality.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.630
I would argue it's the opposite.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.910
When I say to people, Here are the actions
you can take.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:48.190
I'm empowering them to do that and better
set themselves up to challenge the status

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:50.020
quo and to demand that change.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:54.520
When we encourage workers to organize and
demand better wages and working conditions,

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.790
we're trying to improve their lives, but we're
also trying to make a systemic change that

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.590
will benefit more than just them.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:04.380
Now, let's talk about some of the specifics
as they apply to me or people that sometimes

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.370
call in or whatever the case may be.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.580
IP Let's talk about taxes.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:14.460
I pay every dollar in taxes that I'm legally
required to pay at a systemic level.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.150
I think we need higher top tax rates.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.840
We should look at taxing capital gains as
income.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.919
We should eliminate the carried interest loophole.

00:05:21.919 --> 00:05:23.940
We should shift the tax burden away from the
poor.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.729
All of these different things at the individual
level.

00:05:27.729 --> 00:05:32.690
Me David Pakman just sending more money to
the IRS and not taking deductions that are

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.590
available to me.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.290
That's not policy.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.940
That it's just that's not the way we do it.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:43.430
My policy opinion is the one I just told you
and I vote for elected officials that would

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:47.160
put that in place for everyone at the individual
level.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:50.639
I'm not going to pay more tax than I'm legally
required to pay.

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:53.350
I'm not going to send money to the IRS for
no reason.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.050
There is no double standard.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:58.360
The problem isn't individual taxpayers.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:03.860
It's the systemic loopholes and tax breaks
that let the wealthy and corporations evade

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:04.860
taxes.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.259
The 529 account for my daughter.

00:06:06.259 --> 00:06:07.770
I'll do this one.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.759
If college costs keep going up as they happen
by the time my daughter is 18.

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:15.919
The colleges I went to would cost over $200,000
a year.

00:06:15.919 --> 00:06:16.919
That's insane.

00:06:16.919 --> 00:06:18.229
Seems can't possibly happen.

00:06:18.229 --> 00:06:20.210
I spoke to Adam Schiff about this.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.110
The student loan industrial complex is a mess.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:27.760
Maybe jobs should not require a college degree,
and that'll put downward pressure on the cost

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:28.760
of college.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.760
Maybe.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.760
Maybe not.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:37.750
But what do I gain by denying my daughter
a 529 account that I can start funding today?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:42.819
I will advocate for change and I will also
do what I think gives me the best insurance

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:43.819
policy.

00:06:43.819 --> 00:06:48.270
She doesn't go to college or she doesn't need
the money from the 529 because we fix the

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.759
cost of college or whatever in 18 years.

00:06:50.759 --> 00:06:55.539
I can change the beneficiary or take the money
out and pay the 10% penalty, whatever.

00:06:55.539 --> 00:06:58.259
Now to an advice example.

00:06:58.259 --> 00:07:02.940
If someone came to me and said, I'm struggling,
I need to make some more money or I want to

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:07.230
make more money, am I going to rant to them
about income inequality, tax loopholes for

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.120
the rich and that we should have universal
basic income?

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.720
Those are systemic ideas.

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:14.420
I would tell them, Have you looked at a side
business?

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:17.850
Is there a certificate you can get to earn
more money at your current job?

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.210
Is your resume updated?

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:21.229
Is there a skill you can monetize?

00:07:21.229 --> 00:07:27.610
There is not a hypocrisy or double standard
between advocating for systemic change and

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:31.039
in the meantime advising people to do what
is best for their families.

00:07:31.039 --> 00:07:35.660
When people we have a caller who called in
and said, I have a transfer, my partner is

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:40.160
trans or my daughter is trans, I live in a
deep red state.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.160
It's getting really ugly.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.180
They're passing all this legislation systemically.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:47.860
We should work in every state to protect trans
people.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.970
At the individual level, I said to them, You've
got to decide for yourself.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:57.410
Do you need to move to a different state if
you're able to in order to do what you think

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.979
is best for your family right now?

00:07:58.979 --> 00:07:59.979
Sure.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:03.560
In 20 years we might effectively protect trans
people in whatever state it was they were

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:04.659
calling from.

00:08:04.659 --> 00:08:08.129
But in the immediate, if your family's in
danger, I'm going to say, no, you've got to

00:08:08.129 --> 00:08:09.129
stay there.

00:08:09.129 --> 00:08:10.430
And of course not.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:11.430
Okay.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.580
Not a double standard.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:15.920
Let's understand the difference between the
systemic and structural and the individual.

